A sequence $\{f_{k}:{k \in\mathbb {Z}}\}$ in $\mathcal{H}$ is called a Bessel sequence for $\mathcal{H}$ if there exists a constant $B > 0$ such that
\begin{eqnarray*}
\sum \limits_{k \in\mathbb {Z}}|\langle f,f_{k} \rangle |^{2}\leq B\|f\|^{2},\hspace{4mm}\forall f\in \mathcal{H}.
